From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: add a tuning file for the OV5648

The software ISP has no per-sensor tuning at all, so every OV5648 falls back
to uncalibrated.yaml:

  Configuration file 'ov5648.yaml' not found for IPA module 'simple',
  falling back to '/usr/share/libcamera/ipa/simple/uncalibrated.yaml'

which leaves the black level to be guessed from the luminance histogram. That
guess is redone whenever the exposure or gain changes, so the black point
follows the scene rather than the sensor.

Pin it instead. Measured on a PineTab 2 with the sensor covered, the raw
10-bit readout floors at 16, so the pedestal is 1024 in the 16-bit units the
tuning file uses - a quarter of the 16 (8-bit) the algorithm otherwise starts
from.

No colour correction matrix: it has to be measured against a colour chart,
and a borrowed matrix is worse than none. The place for it is left documented
in the file.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
diff -ruN tu_a/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build tu_b/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build	2026-09-18 19:06:58.756687466 +0200
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build	2026-09-18 19:06:58.778036754 +0200
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
 
 conf_files = files([
+    'ov5648.yaml',
     'uncalibrated.yaml',
 ])
 
diff -ruN tu_a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml tu_b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml	1970-01-01 01:00:00.000000000 +0100
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/ov5648.yaml	2026-09-18 19:06:58.765052712 +0200
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
+%YAML 1.1
+---
+version: 1
+algorithms:
+  - BlackLevel:
+      # Measured on a PineTab 2: with the sensor covered the raw 10-bit
+      # readout floors at 16, so the pedestal is 16/1023 -> 1024 in the
+      # 16-bit units this file uses. Without a value here the algorithm
+      # guesses from the luminance histogram every time the exposure or
+      # gain changes, which makes the black point follow the scene.
+      blackLevel: 1024
+  - Awb:
+  # A colour correction matrix belongs here, but it has to be measured -
+  # a borrowed or invented matrix is worse than none at all, and the CCM
+  # algorithm is expensive enough that it should only be switched on once
+  # it is tuned. Generate one with utils/tuning against a colour chart and
+  # add it as:
+  #
+  #   - Ccm:
+  #       ccms:
+  #         - ct: 6500
+  #           ccm: [ ... ]
+  - Adjust:
+  - Agc:
+...
